#+auto_tangle: t

This file is the SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH for early-init.el and
foundation-init.el.

*How it works:*
- On every save of THIS FILE, org-auto-tangle regenerates both
  targets automatically (it only fires for files carrying the
  ~#+auto_tangle: t~ property above).
- At every startup, the static seed ~init.el~ tangles this file
  again (belt and suspenders) and then loads the freshly generated
  ~foundation-init.el~.
- ~early-init.el~ is loaded by Emacs BEFORE init.el, so it can be at
  most one save stale — it only holds visual/palette setup, so that
  staleness is harmless.
- Never edit ~early-init.el~ or ~foundation-init.el~ directly — they
  are build artifacts.

*Why this lives inside Cyberdeck-Emacs/:*
Everything here must run before the loader processes ~modules~.
Putting it in a module would be circular (the boot system isn't
loaded yet) — so it sits beside the module tree it boots: the whole
subsystem in one directory.

